\section{Introduction}
Matu Daro Melanau (ISO 639-3 \texttt{dro}; Glottocode daro1239) is an Austronesian language of the Melanau group in Sarawak, Malaysia. Speaker counts in sources conflict (7,600 from a 1981 citation; Joshua Project lists 23,000 people).
\section{Primary Educational Resources}
None found in search results.
\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, ``Daro-Matu language''. \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daro-Matu_language}
\item Wikipedia, ``Melanau language'' (the wider Melanau language). \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Melanau_language}
\item Bernama (2019) report on a Melanau--Malay dictionary covering the Matu, Daro and Pulau Bruit areas, compiled by UNESCO, Dewan Bahasa dan Pustaka and the Education Ministry; publication was then expected the following year. Whether it appeared was not confirmed. \url{https://www.bernama.com/en/news.php?id=1774706}
\end{itemize}
\section{Religious and Community Resources}
\begin{itemize}
\item Joshua Project, Daro-Matu in Malaysia: population data; notes Scripture and teaching materials are not yet available. \url{https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/11509}
\end{itemize}
\section{Digital and Audio Resources}
None found in search results.
\section{Curriculum Development Context}
No school curriculum materials were found. The dictionary project mentioned above, if completed, would be a starting point; the status should be checked with Dewan Bahasa dan Pustaka.
\end{document}
